WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.667 --> 00:00:04.901
-The governor of Flordia berated a bunch of high school students

00:00:04.901 --> 00:00:07.334
for wearing masks while Fox News continued

00:00:07.334 --> 00:00:09.667
to attack President Biden's response to the Russian

00:00:09.667 --> 00:00:11.734
invasion of Ukraine and criticized him

00:00:11.734 --> 00:00:14.701
for not singing "Happy Birthday" at the State of the Union.

00:00:14.701 --> 00:00:17.267
For more on this, it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:17.267 --> 00:00:19.267
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:20.968 --> 00:00:22.968
If you want to be a successful Republican

00:00:22.968 --> 00:00:24.901
politician these days, you have to follow

00:00:24.901 --> 00:00:27.334
"The Donald Trump Playbook," which is being a loud

00:00:27.334 --> 00:00:29.033
and obnoxious ass-(bleep) in public.

00:00:29.033 --> 00:00:30.767
In fact, if you open the "Playbook,"

00:00:30.767 --> 00:00:33.400
it's just his mouth rambling about nonsense.

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:37.033
-People are flushing toilets ten times, 15 times,

00:00:37.033 --> 00:00:39.000
as opposed to once.

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:41.067
[ Laughter ]

00:00:41.067 --> 00:00:43.601
That's also the first time I saw that.

00:00:45.334 --> 00:00:46.834
That's Donald Trump's whole schtick --

00:00:46.834 --> 00:00:49.167
a thing that made him a star with Republican voters.

00:00:49.167 --> 00:00:50.601
He just goes from town to town

00:00:50.601 --> 00:00:52.300
holding his one-man "Wrestlemanias,"

00:00:52.300 --> 00:00:54.100
where he just loudly whines and rants,

00:00:54.100 --> 00:00:55.934
and his crowd chants "lock them up"

00:00:55.934 --> 00:00:57.167
even when it doesn't make any sense.

00:00:57.167 --> 00:00:59.267
Just once, I would love for them to chant that

00:00:59.267 --> 00:01:00.701
in a legitimately helpful way.

00:01:00.701 --> 00:01:02.934
It could be helpful, like when you're going away

00:01:02.934 --> 00:01:04.734
for the weekend and leaving your teen son

00:01:04.734 --> 00:01:05.734
in charge of the house.

00:01:05.734 --> 00:01:07.067
"Hey, honey, what should I do

00:01:07.067 --> 00:01:08.567
with all the liquor and edibles?"

00:01:11.934 --> 00:01:13.801
-Thank you.

00:01:13.801 --> 00:01:16.467
That was helpful.

00:01:16.467 --> 00:01:18.567
That's the heart of modern Republican politics,

00:01:18.567 --> 00:01:20.167
and that's what was going on yesterday,

00:01:20.167 --> 00:01:21.934
when Florida Governor Ron DeSantis showed up

00:01:21.934 --> 00:01:24.734
to a press conference at the University of South Florida

00:01:24.734 --> 00:01:26.901
and scolded a bunch of high school students

00:01:26.901 --> 00:01:28.701
for wearing masks.

00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:32.133
[ Laughter ]

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:41.834
[ Sighs ]

00:01:41.834 --> 00:01:44.067
All right, well, it's good to be at USF.

00:01:44.067 --> 00:01:45.334
-Is it?

00:01:45.334 --> 00:01:46.834
[ Laughter ]

00:01:47.968 --> 00:01:51.334
Because you certainly don't seem happy to be there.

00:01:51.334 --> 00:01:52.968
It's like when I go in for a root canal

00:01:52.968 --> 00:01:55.067
and my dentist says, "Hey, good to see you."

00:01:55.067 --> 00:01:57.434
And I say, "Yeah, good to be here."

00:01:57.434 --> 00:01:58.501
[ Laughter ]

00:01:58.501 --> 00:02:00.100
How much of a dick do you have to be

00:02:00.100 --> 00:02:01.834
to yell at a bunch of high school students

00:02:01.834 --> 00:02:02.934
who are just trying to be safe?

00:02:02.934 --> 00:02:04.534
They're actually doing the right thing,

00:02:04.534 --> 00:02:05.834
and you're scolding them for it.

00:02:05.834 --> 00:02:07.234
You're like an old man who sees a bunch

00:02:07.234 --> 00:02:10.300
of innocent teens walking by and screams, "Hey, you kids!

00:02:10.300 --> 00:02:12.501
Get on my lawn!

00:02:12.501 --> 00:02:14.567
And while you're at it, throw a frisbee through my window!

00:02:14.567 --> 00:02:16.133
It's not a trap."

00:02:16.133 --> 00:02:17.934
Also, let's just establish the facts here.

00:02:17.934 --> 00:02:20.667
DeSantis is obviously wrong, and masks absolutely help

00:02:20.667 --> 00:02:22.000
control the spread of COVID.

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:23.834
Studies have repeatedly proven that over and over again,

00:02:23.834 --> 00:02:25.701
and the better the mask, the better protection.

00:02:25.701 --> 00:02:28.100
Ideally, everyone should have access to high hquality,

00:02:28.100 --> 00:02:30.968
high filtration, medical-grade masks like N95s,

00:02:30.968 --> 00:02:34.400
KN95s, KF94s, and my personal favorite,

00:02:34.400 --> 00:02:36.601
the AC360, which makes the bottom half of your face

00:02:36.601 --> 00:02:38.267
look like Anderson Cooper's.

00:02:38.267 --> 00:02:40.567
[ Laughter ]

00:02:40.567 --> 00:02:43.167
Sure, the top half of my face ruins it.

00:02:44.167 --> 00:02:45.901
Also, what the hell is "COVID theater"?

00:02:45.901 --> 00:02:47.367
Are those plays where all the actors

00:02:47.367 --> 00:02:48.801
have to stand six feet apart?

00:02:48.801 --> 00:02:51.234
"I just saw the COVID Theater production of "'Les Mis.'

00:02:51.234 --> 00:02:53.968
The stage was the size of a football field."

00:02:54.968 --> 00:02:56.868
And yet, it won't surprise you to learn

00:02:56.868 --> 00:02:58.601
that he was celebrated later that night

00:02:58.601 --> 00:03:01.200
by a host on Fox News, who thought it was hilarious

00:03:01.200 --> 00:03:02.767
that he yelled at a bunch of teenagers

00:03:02.767 --> 00:03:04.734
who are trying to stay safe and do the right thing.

00:03:04.734 --> 00:03:07.167
-Raymond, the best is Ron DeSantis

00:03:07.167 --> 00:03:08.734
telling those kids, "Get your masks off."

00:03:08.734 --> 00:03:09.901
I love that.

00:03:09.901 --> 00:03:12.100
People are all upset about Ron DeSantis today.

00:03:12.100 --> 00:03:14.901
Someone has to tell these kids

00:03:14.901 --> 00:03:18.767
to push away all of the brainwashing

00:03:18.767 --> 00:03:20.300
that they have been subject to.

00:03:20.300 --> 00:03:22.534
-What kind of adult laughs at another adult

00:03:22.534 --> 00:03:23.934
yelling at a bunch of kids?

00:03:23.934 --> 00:03:27.467
What -- If you've ever seen an 80s comedy,

00:03:27.467 --> 00:03:28.701
you know it's the opposite.

00:03:28.701 --> 00:03:31.467
It's funny when teens get the best of adults.

00:03:31.467 --> 00:03:33.000
I mean, if Ferris Bueller skipped school

00:03:33.000 --> 00:03:34.834
and the principal found him and suspended him,

00:03:34.834 --> 00:03:36.234
that's not a movie.

00:03:36.234 --> 00:03:38.400
"Animal House" didn't end with the Dean expelling everyone

00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:39.801
and turning the house into a rec center.

00:03:39.801 --> 00:03:41.767
In fact, if you recall, Bluto became a senator.

00:03:41.767 --> 00:03:43.467
Oh, you don't recall, because you were all born

00:03:43.467 --> 00:03:44.634
20 years after that movie came out?

00:03:44.634 --> 00:03:46.033
All right.

00:03:46.033 --> 00:03:48.267
Well, in that case, give it up for "Euphoria," everybody.

00:03:48.267 --> 00:03:49.901
"Euphoria."

00:03:49.901 --> 00:03:52.567
There we go.

00:03:52.567 --> 00:03:54.834
And that was today's cheap applause line.

00:03:56.467 --> 00:03:59.367
The DeSantis tirade was an interesting juxtaposition

00:03:59.367 --> 00:04:01.634
with the State of the Union on Tuesday, where Joe Biden

00:04:01.634 --> 00:04:04.033
introduced 13-year-old Joshua Davis,

00:04:04.033 --> 00:04:06.734
who has Type 1 diabetes and has spent years

00:04:06.734 --> 00:04:09.234
raising awareness and advocating for lowering the costs

00:04:09.234 --> 00:04:10.901
of insulin and prescription drugs.

00:04:10.901 --> 00:04:13.701
It also happened to be the day after his birthday,

00:04:13.701 --> 00:04:15.033
which Biden pointed out.

00:04:15.033 --> 00:04:17.534
-Joshua is here tonight, but yesterday was his birthday.

00:04:17.534 --> 00:04:19.267
Happy birthday, buddy, by the way.

00:04:19.267 --> 00:04:21.501
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:21.501 --> 00:04:23.234
-Or, as Ron DeSantis would say,

00:04:23.234 --> 00:04:25.234
"Yesterday was his birthday, not today.

00:04:25.234 --> 00:04:27.300
I don't want to see anyone wishing him a happy birthday.

00:04:27.300 --> 00:04:29.767
We have to stop with this birthday theater.

00:04:31.300 --> 00:04:33.901
Anyway, it's good to be at your party, Joshua."

00:04:33.901 --> 00:04:35.968
[ Laughter ]

00:04:35.968 --> 00:04:38.467
Imagine how cool it must be to tell your friends

00:04:38.467 --> 00:04:40.634
you had your birthday party at the State of the Union.

00:04:40.634 --> 00:04:42.434
Although personally, I still think

00:04:42.434 --> 00:04:43.567
I would prefer Chuck E. Cheese.

00:04:43.567 --> 00:04:44.834
That's just me.

00:04:44.834 --> 00:04:47.300
But let's not forget, the State of the Union

00:04:47.300 --> 00:04:49.601
did have an animatronic Chuck there,

00:04:49.601 --> 00:04:52.634
but I think his wiring was all, like, (bleep) up.

00:04:52.634 --> 00:04:55.601
[ Robotic whirring, sizzling ]

00:04:55.601 --> 00:04:57.701
[ Laughter ]

00:04:57.701 --> 00:04:58.834
Anyway...

00:05:01.367 --> 00:05:03.934
In these polarizing times, it was nice to have a sweet,

00:05:03.934 --> 00:05:05.901
unifying moment everyone could get behind.

00:05:05.901 --> 00:05:08.868
I mean, who could possibly quibble with that moment?

00:05:08.868 --> 00:05:10.200
Oh -- Oh, no.

00:05:10.200 --> 00:05:12.234
We're about to play a Fox News clip, aren't we?

00:05:12.234 --> 00:05:14.167
All right. -The young kid who has --

00:05:14.167 --> 00:05:17.567
suffers from the diabetes and needs his insulin.

00:05:17.567 --> 00:05:18.767
Loved that.

00:05:18.767 --> 00:05:20.200
But again, even there was that missed moment

00:05:20.200 --> 00:05:21.534
for humanity, right?

00:05:21.534 --> 00:05:23.934
The president says, "And it was his birthday yesterday."

00:05:23.934 --> 00:05:26.467
Well, then, clue.

00:05:26.467 --> 00:05:27.868
Sing "Happy Birthday."

00:05:27.868 --> 00:05:28.868
That's what we do.

00:05:28.868 --> 00:05:30.033
Have a human moment.

00:05:30.033 --> 00:05:32.534
-Yeah, that's what we do.

00:05:32.534 --> 00:05:38.033
We sing "Happy Birthday" the day after people's birthday.

00:05:38.033 --> 00:05:39.934
Sorry, this might be the funniest criticism

00:05:39.934 --> 00:05:41.834
of a president I've ever heard.

00:05:41.834 --> 00:05:44.534
"He addressed the crisis in Ukraine and rising inflation,

00:05:44.534 --> 00:05:46.400
but I did miss hearing 'Happy Birthday.'

00:05:46.400 --> 00:05:48.834
Look, I'm not saying I needed the whole,

00:05:48.834 --> 00:05:50.868
'how old are you now' verse -- that would have been overkill.

00:05:50.868 --> 00:05:52.100
But where was the song?

00:05:52.100 --> 00:05:53.767
I feel as though -- clue --

00:05:53.767 --> 00:05:56.200
we're a country without a leader."

00:05:56.200 --> 00:05:58.501
And yet, somehow, that was not the weirdest thing

00:05:58.501 --> 00:06:00.434
a Fox News personality said yesterday,

00:06:00.434 --> 00:06:04.100
because FOX host Sean Hannity touted what he apparently thinks

00:06:04.100 --> 00:06:07.300
is a brilliant idea for a new military strategy in Ukraine.

00:06:07.300 --> 00:06:10.033
As you may know, NATO and the US have been explicit

00:06:10.033 --> 00:06:12.033
about the fact that they want to support Ukraine

00:06:12.033 --> 00:06:14.968
while avoiding direct military conflict with Russia,

00:06:14.968 --> 00:06:17.334
since that could very easily spiral out of control

00:06:17.334 --> 00:06:18.968
into a massive global confrontation

00:06:18.968 --> 00:06:19.968
between nuclear powers.

00:06:19.968 --> 00:06:21.901
But Hannity has an idea

00:06:21.901 --> 00:06:23.200
to get around all that --

00:06:23.200 --> 00:06:24.667
bomb a Russian convoy,

00:06:24.667 --> 00:06:26.868
but then just don't tell them who did it.

00:06:48.200 --> 00:06:49.834
Why hasn't anybody --

00:06:49.834 --> 00:06:52.133
You don't have to take credit for it.

00:06:52.133 --> 00:06:54.501
But there is something called a covert operation

00:06:54.501 --> 00:06:56.701
with plausible deniability.

00:06:56.701 --> 00:06:59.334
Why hasn't any European country stepped up?

00:06:59.334 --> 00:07:01.167
They're sitting ducks right now.

00:07:01.167 --> 00:07:04.400
Take out that convoy and prevent that massacre.

00:07:04.400 --> 00:07:05.901
-That's a brilliant idea, Sean.

00:07:05.901 --> 00:07:08.434
We just bomb Russia, but then don't tell them it was us.

00:07:08.434 --> 00:07:10.801
And since Russia doesn't have satellites or video cameras

00:07:10.801 --> 00:07:13.567
or cellphones or eyes, they'll have no way of knowing.

00:07:13.567 --> 00:07:15.767
Maybe we can just paint the "Republic of Updog"

00:07:15.767 --> 00:07:19.267
on the side of all of our jets, and then Putin will say,

00:07:19.267 --> 00:07:20.934
"What's updog?" And we'll all say,

00:07:20.934 --> 00:07:23.334
"I don't know, what's up with you?"

00:07:24.434 --> 00:07:26.501
[ Laughs ] And then, even he would have to laugh,

00:07:26.501 --> 00:07:29.234
and life will go back to normal.

00:07:29.234 --> 00:07:32.701
[ Russian accent ] "Oh, you got me very well."

00:07:32.701 --> 00:07:35.434
Also worth noting that things are so crazy,

00:07:35.434 --> 00:07:39.701
we barely have time to point out that Dr. Oz was in that clip,

00:07:39.701 --> 00:07:41.934
and he's just fully running for Senate.

00:07:41.934 --> 00:07:45.234
You see it, and you shrug and think, "Yeah, why not?

00:07:45.234 --> 00:07:47.067
Why not? Dr. Oz for Senate. Great."

00:07:47.067 --> 00:07:48.834
At this point, if you heard the chief negotiator

00:07:48.834 --> 00:07:52.067
between Russia and Ukraine was Dr. Phil, would you even blink?

00:07:52.067 --> 00:07:54.300
"Vlad, you need to accept that the person

00:07:54.300 --> 00:07:58.467
you're really hurting with this war is Vlad."

00:07:59.868 --> 00:08:01.501
I don't have a good Dr. Phil

00:08:01.501 --> 00:08:05.534
because there's no such thing as a good Dr. Phil.

00:08:05.534 --> 00:08:07.200
The GOP playbook these days

00:08:07.200 --> 00:08:10.133
is just being a loud, obnoxious jerk in public.

00:08:10.133 --> 00:08:12.100
That's the main thing you have to do in order to succeed

00:08:12.100 --> 00:08:13.434
as a Republican politician.

00:08:13.434 --> 00:08:15.067
People like Lauren Boebert, Marjorie Taylor Greene,

00:08:15.067 --> 00:08:16.801
and Ron DeSantis keep proving that.

00:08:16.801 --> 00:08:18.667
And we know who they learned it from.

00:08:18.667 --> 00:08:19.868
They learned it from Trump.

00:08:19.868 --> 00:08:21.701
It's not a mystery. This isn't a game of...

00:08:21.701 --> 00:08:22.701
-Clue.

00:08:22.701 --> 00:08:25.334
[ Laughter ]

00:08:30.801 --> 00:08:33.300
Not sure about that one. [ Laughing ]

00:08:33.300 --> 00:08:35.434
This has been "A Closer Look."

